---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Admin
    participant Page as Admin sites page<br/>/admin/sites
    participant Archived as Archived sites page<br/>/admin/sites/archived
    participant Actions as Server actions<br/>utils/supabase/queries.ts
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL

    Note over Admin,DB: Covers US 2.0.4. The team chose archive over a hard delete (#160). "Delete" archives the Site.<br/>An Admin can then restore it or delete it permanently from the archived list.<br/>Every action calls requireApprovedAdmin() first. The RPCs run with the service role client.

    rect rgb(240, 245, 255)
    Note over Admin,DB: Archive a Site
    Admin->>Page: Select "Archive site" on a Site
    activate Page
    Page->>Actions: getSiteDeleteImpact(siteId)
    activate Actions
    Actions->>Actions: requireApprovedAdmin()
    Actions->>DB: rpc get_site_delete_impact(p_site_id)
    activate DB
    DB-->>Actions: Counts of SIRs, answers, attachments, homepage images and steward assignments
    deactivate DB
    Actions-->>Page: SiteDeleteImpact
    deactivate Actions
    Page-->>Admin: Ask to confirm. Name the number of affected records (AT1, AT2)

    alt Admin cancels
        Admin->>Page: Select Cancel
        Page-->>Admin: Close the dialog. Nothing changes.
    else Admin confirms
        Admin->>Page: Select "Archive Site"
        Page->>Actions: archiveSite(siteId)
        activate Actions
        Actions->>Actions: requireApprovedAdmin()
        alt Caller is not an approved Admin
            Actions-->>Page: Error "Only admins can edit sites."
            Page-->>Admin: Show the error. Nothing changes.
        else Caller is an approved Admin
            Actions->>DB: rpc archive_site(p_site_id)<br/>one transaction, row locked: set sites_pa.archived_at = now()
            activate DB
            alt Site is missing or already archived (AT4)
                DB-->>Actions: Error. Nothing is changed.
                Actions-->>Page: Error message
                Page-->>Admin: Show the error. The Site and all records are unchanged.
            else Archived
                DB-->>Actions: siteId, siteName, archivedAt
                deactivate DB
                Actions-->>Page: SiteArchiveResult
                Page-->>Admin: Remove the Site from the list and add 1 to the Archived count
            end
        end
        deactivate Actions
    end
    deactivate Page
    Note over Admin,DB: Archiving deletes nothing. SIRs, answers, attachments, homepage images and the steward assignment<br/>stay connected to the Site (AT3). getSitesOnline, getAllSites and getCurrentSiteId filter on archived_at is null,<br/>so the Site leaves the site lists and takes no new SIR until it is restored.
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
    Note over Admin,DB: Restore an archived Site
    Admin->>Archived: Open "Archived" and select Restore on a Site
    activate Archived
    Archived->>Actions: getArchivedSites() when the page loads
    Actions-->>Archived: SiteSummary[] with archived_at
    Archived->>Actions: restoreSite(siteId)
    activate Actions
    Actions->>Actions: requireApprovedAdmin()
    Actions->>DB: rpc restore_site(p_site_id): set archived_at = null
    DB-->>Actions: siteId, siteName (error if the Site is not archived)
    Actions-->>Archived: SiteRestoreResult
    deactivate Actions
    Archived-->>Admin: Remove the Site from the archived list. It shows on /admin/sites again.
    deactivate Archived
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 240)
    Note over Admin,DB: Permanently delete an archived Site
    Admin->>Archived: Select "Permanently delete" on an archived Site
    activate Archived
    Archived->>Actions: getSiteDeleteImpact(siteId)
    Actions->>DB: rpc get_site_delete_impact(p_site_id)
    DB-->>Actions: Counts
    Actions-->>Archived: SiteDeleteImpact
    Archived-->>Admin: Ask to confirm. Name the records that will be disconnected (AT1, AT2).<br/>The dialog says this cannot be undone.
    alt Admin cancels
        Admin->>Archived: Select Cancel
        Archived-->>Admin: Close the dialog. Nothing changes.
    else Admin confirms
        Admin->>Archived: Select confirm
        Archived->>Actions: permanentlyDeleteSite(siteId)
        activate Actions
        Actions->>Actions: requireApprovedAdmin()
        Actions->>DB: rpc permanently_delete_site(p_site_id)<br/>one transaction, row locked
        activate DB
        alt Site is missing or not archived (AT4)
            DB-->>Actions: Error. Nothing is changed.
            Actions-->>Archived: Error message
            Archived-->>Admin: Show the error. The Site and all records are unchanged.
        else Archived Site
            DB->>DB: Set site_id = NULL on form_responses, attachments and homepage_image_uploads.<br/>Delete the sites_pa row. site_stewards and site_page_fields rows go by cascade.
            DB-->>Actions: Counts from before the delete
            deactivate DB
            Actions-->>Archived: SiteDeleteImpact
            Archived-->>Admin: Remove the Site from the archived list
        end
        deactivate Actions
    end
    deactivate Archived
    Note over Admin,DB: Only the Site row, its steward assignment and its page fields are removed. SIRs, answers, attachments<br/>and homepage images stay in the database with no Site, and their S3 files are not deleted.<br/>protected_areas and people rows are not touched.
    end
